  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "The genus-2 antivortex: finding the over-agreeing face is PPADS-complete",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Let G_a be the double of the holed lattice torus T(3a Z^2) along a hexagonal hole: a closed orientable genus-2 surface whose incidence graph has six four-corner faces (the hexagon's corners, degree 8) and three-corner faces elsewhere, with the Kasteleyn signs of COUNT-SURFACES-20261107-001A. (1) The frames of FLAT-STATES-20261107-001A are flat around three-corner faces and turn by label +1 around each four-corner face, the mirror of the knot sphere's -1. (2) For exactly one of the 16 Kasteleyn classes the handle loops are flat; cutting along six disjoint chart-confined paths from a point z to the four-corner faces and developing one frame gives an assignment with no violated line and exactly one over-agreeing face, at z. (3) Placing FLAT-STATES-20261107-001B's Sperner map in a region around z, the region's boundary is the canonical Sperner boundary with colours 1 and 2 swapped, and over-agreeing faces sit exactly one in each clockwise fully labelled triangle, violated lines exactly one in each counterclockwise one. (4) Hence finding an over-agreeing face of the knot on G_a, a total problem since over-agreement minus violated lines is 1, is PPADS^dt-complete, and finding a violated line or an over-agreeing face is PPAD^dt-complete, while the knot's lines alone are satisfiable.",
  "dependencies": [
    "COUNT-SURFACES-20261107-001Z",
    "COUNT-TFNP-20261107-001Z",
    "FLAT-STATES-20261107-001Z"
  ],
  "evidence_modes": [
